            <ArticleTitle>Global pollution by organochlorinated endocrine disruptors - possible challenge for mankind at the onset of millennium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25-36</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Author of this review submits a comprehensive report of his long-lasting research regarding the global pollution by endocrine disruptors (EDs), EDs and diabetes and obesity, EDs and the thyroid in highly polluted Slovakia, Ah-receptor: the central pivot responsible for such global &quot;EDs disaster&quot;, EDs and immune system, EDs and testosterone, EDs in mothers and newborns, EDs and human genome, and EDs at the beginning of the millennium.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
